================================================================================
Methods, conventions and attribution
================================================================================

Asymmetry is a Python toolkit for muon-spin spectroscopy (μSR) data analysis.
Its analysis methods, fit models, workflows and file-format support draw on the
μSR literature and established μSR programs. References include publications,
manuals, documented formats, observed behaviour and source-level study.

The acknowledgements below describe these references and the conventions they
inform. They do not grant permission to redistribute another project's code
under Asymmetry's MIT licence. Published method comparisons and their validation
scope are described at
https://benhuddart.github.io/asymmetry/explanation/comparison.html.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WiMDA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A freely available muon-spin-spectroscopy data-analysis program by Francis L.
Pratt (ISIS Muon Group).
Copyright (c) 2000-2022 Francis Pratt and ISIS Rutherford Appleton Laboratory.

Asymmetry includes WiMDA-derived fit-function and detector-balance conventions,
a radical line-pair combiner, a comparison mode for rotating-frame display,
and a zero-frequency spectral-background convention.
Its count- and frequency-domain workflows also follow conventions described
by WiMDA. The applicable rights in WiMDA and its fitting libraries remain with their
respective rights holders.

  F. L. Pratt, "WiMDA: a muon data analysis program for the Windows PC",
  Physica B 289-290, 710-714 (2000).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
musrfit
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
An open-source μSR fitting framework by Andreas Suter, Bastian Wojek and
contributors, distributed under the GNU General Public License. Asymmetry's
PSI-BIN/MDU and MusrRoot support, instrument groupings, fitting conventions and
asymmetry-balance conventions refer to musrfit's formats, documentation, source
and observed behaviour. The applicable licence version and terms accompany the
musrfit distribution.

  A. Suter and B. M. Wojek, "Musrfit: A Free Platform-Independent Framework for
  muSR Data Analysis", Physics Procedia 30, 69-73 (2012).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mantid
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
An open-source data-reduction and analysis framework distributed under the GNU
General Public License v3 or later. Asymmetry's NeXus muon loading,
asymmetry/alpha conventions, deadtime handling, integral field-scan workflows
and MaxEnt pulse-response comparisons refer to Mantid's formats, documentation,
source and observed behaviour.

  O. Arnold et al., "Mantid - Data analysis and visualization package for
  neutron scattering and muSR experiments", Nucl. Instrum. Methods A 764,
  156-166 (2014).

